{"kind":"report","text":"LS-7 route check (8500587f). You are right: the in-place route in ea4be750 fails in lending-shelf. I withdraw it.\n\nRules version: 15. The fast read is `dap verify rules` from the operator home, which took about 3 s. Its trust list names `platform:rules@15` and `platform:directory@27`, the `base` cohort row in docs/cli.md:174. (`dap show rules:0` also answers in under 3 s, but it does not name the definition.) Rules 15 has no upgrade-application act, in either form.\n\nDoes any act move an existing room to Rules 16? No. A scope's definition changes only by succession, and docs/roadmap.md:51 and :78 say succession is designed, not built. Route (a) or (b) is needed.\n\n(a) A new installation item in lending-shelf.\nSteps:\n1. `dap application install` of Lending 0.5.0 (1bda4e9b, trusted) from the operator home. Rules 15 has install-application, and I find no refusal of a second installation of the same application. The counter-witness room holds many Counter items.\n2. The operator donates the stepladder again in the new Library scope.\n3. A SCREEN_HOSTS head moves lending-shelf.inguz.space to the new item, with a full gate and your sandbox deployment.\n4. A second invitation, and the rerun with a persistent profile.\nResidue: item 2 and its Library scope stay active, with the first stepladder and the published shelf page. @shelf-witness and key_rz2EhUy0 stay as they are.\nWhat it witnesses: GW-1's browser half on the live shelf host. It does not witness an upgrade.\n\n(b) A new room under the `upgrade` cohort.\nSteps:\n1. You create the room on dap-lending with `--cohort upgrade` and make a new operator home.\n2. Install Lending 0.4.0, or 0.5.0 directly.\n3. Donate the stepladder.\n4. A SCREEN_HOSTS head for a new host, or a move of lending-shelf.inguz.space, with a gate and a deployment.\n5. An invitation and the run.\nIf you install 0.4.0 and upgrade in place to 0.5.0 before the join, the same room also gives Lending's in-place witness, the Lending twin of U4.\nResidue: a whole room: register, Directory, Membership, Rules, Destination and Library objects, with their archive alarms. The read of the wake rate in that review must name the added requests per hour. lending-shelf also stays as it is.\n\nRecommendation: (a). LS-7 asks for the live shelf room behind lending-shelf.inguz.space, and (a) keeps that room and that host. Its residue is one installation item, not a room. It has one fewer creation step and no new wake-rate floor. U4 already gives the in-place witness on Counter in an upgrade-cohort room, so a Lending twin from (b) adds a second example of the same path, not new coverage. If you want Lending's in-place witness anyway, the U4 room could hold a Lending install beside the Counter one, with no new room. I file the screen-host head for (a) as soon as you hand me the new item number. I hold the LS-7 rerun until after the U4 gate (running now, 63841108).","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}